# Environment Variables for Payment Integration

This file documents all environment variables required for payment integration. Copy this to `.env.local` and fill in your actual values.

## Stripe Configuration
```
# Stripe API Key (Publishable - safe for frontend)
# Get from: https://dashboard.stripe.com/apikeys
REACT_APP_STRIPE_PUBLIC_KEY=pk_test_YOUR_PUBLISHABLE_KEY_HERE

# Stripe Buy Button ID
# Get from: https://dashboard.stripe.com/payment-links (Buy Button section)
REACT_APP_STRIPE_BUY_BUTTON_ID=buy_btn_YOUR_BUY_BUTTON_ID_HERE

# Stripe Webhook Secret (Backend only)
# Get from: https://dashboard.stripe.com/webhooks
REACT_APP_STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_YOUR_WEBHOOK_SECRET_HERE
```

## PayPal Configuration
```
# PayPal Client ID (safe for frontend)
# Get from: https://www.paypal.com/cgi-bin/webscr?cmd=_account-server-accounts
REACT_APP_PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID=YOUR_SANDBOX_CLIENT_ID_HERE

# PayPal Environment (sandbox or production)
# Start with 'sandbox' for testing
REACT_APP_PAYPAL_ENV=sandbox

# PayPal Webhook ID (Backend only)
# Get from: https://www.paypal.com/cgi-bin/webscr?cmd=_account-webhooks
REACT_APP_PAYPAL_WEBHOOK_ID=YOUR_WEBHOOK_ID_HERE
```

## Apple Pay Configuration
```
# Apple Pay Merchant ID
# Register at: https://developer.apple.com
REACT_APP_APPLE_PAY_MERCHANT_ID=merchant.com.naacus
```

## Google Pay Configuration
```
# Google Pay Merchant ID (Google Cloud Project ID)
# Get from: https://console.cloud.google.com
REACT_APP_GOOGLE_PAY_MERCHANT_ID=YOUR_MERCHANT_ID_HERE

# Google Pay Environment (TEST or PRODUCTION)
# Use TEST for development/testing
REACT_APP_GOOGLE_PAY_ENV=TEST
```

## Cryptocurrency Configuration
```
# Cryptocurrency Webhook Secret (Backend only)
# Generate a secure random string
REACT_APP_CRYPTO_WEBHOOK_SECRET=your_secure_webhook_secret_here

# Cryptocurrency Provider (coinbase or bitpay)
# Default: coinbase
REACT_APP_CRYPTO_PROVIDER=coinbase
```

## Cash App / Square Configuration
```
# Square Application ID
# Get from: https://developer.squareup.com/apps
REACT_APP_SQUARE_APPLICATION_ID=YOUR_SQUARE_APP_ID_HERE

# Square Location ID
# Get from: https://dashboard.squareup.com/locations
REACT_APP_SQUARE_LOCATION_ID=YOUR_SQUARE_LOCATION_ID_HERE

# Square Webhook Secret (Backend only)
# Get from: https://developer.squareup.com/apps/webhooks
REACT_APP_SQUARE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=YOUR_SQUARE_WEBHOOK_SECRET_HERE
```

## Backend API Configuration
```
# API Base URL
# Development: http://localhost:3001/api/v1
# Production: https://your-api-domain.com/api/v1
REACT_APP_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3001/api/v1
```

## Getting Started

### 1. Stripe Setup
```bash
# Visit Stripe Dashboard
https://dashboard.stripe.com/

# In API keys section:
# - Copy your publishable key (starts with pk_test_ or pk_live_)
# - Paste into REACT_APP_STRIPE_PUBLIC_KEY

# In Webhooks section:
# - Create webhook endpoint
# - Copy signing secret
# - Paste into REACT_APP_STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET
```

### 2. PayPal Setup
```bash
# Visit PayPal Developer
https://developer.paypal.com/

# In Applications:
# - Create new app
# - Copy Client ID
# - Paste into REACT_APP_PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID

# Set environment:
# - Use 'sandbox' for testing
# - Use 'production' for live
```

### 3. Apple Pay Setup
```bash
# Visit Apple Developer
https://developer.apple.com/

# Register merchant:
# - Go to Certificates, Identifiers & Profiles
# - Register new merchant ID
# - Format: merchant.com.naacus
```

### 4. Google Pay Setup
```bash
# Visit Google Cloud Console
https://console.cloud.google.com/

# Enable payments:
# - Enable Google Pay API
# - Create merchant ID
# - Copy to REACT_APP_GOOGLE_PAY_MERCHANT_ID
```

### 5. Cryptocurrency Setup
```bash
# Visit Coinbase Commerce
https://commerce.coinbase.com/

# Create merchant account:
# - Sign up for account
# - Go to Settings -> Webhooks
# - Create webhook endpoint
# - Copy shared secret
# - Paste into REACT_APP_CRYPTO_WEBHOOK_SECRET
```

### 6. Cash App / Square Setup
```bash
# Visit Square Developer Dashboard
https://developer.squareup.com/

# Create application:
# - Create new application
# - Copy Application ID
# - Paste into REACT_APP_SQUARE_APPLICATION_ID

# Get Location ID:
# - Go to Locations
# - Copy your Location ID
# - Paste into REACT_APP_SQUARE_LOCATION_ID

# Set up webhooks:
# - Go to Webhooks settings
# - Create webhook endpoint
# - Copy signing secret
# - Paste into REACT_APP_SQUARE_WEBHOOK_SECRET
```
# For Coinbase Commerce
https://commerce.coinbase.com/

# For BitPay
https://bitpay.com/

# Generate webhook secret:
openssl rand -hex 32
# Paste output into REACT_APP_CRYPTO_WEBHOOK_SECRET
```

## Testing Payment Methods

### Test Card Numbers (Stripe)
```
Visa:        4242 4242 4242 4242
Mastercard:  5555 5555 5555 4444
Amex:        3782 822463 10005
Discover:    6011 1111 1111 1117
Declined:    4000 0000 0000 0002
```

### Test Mode Limits
- Amount can be anything
- Future expiry dates work
- Any 3-digit CVC works
- For 3D Secure, any OTP code works

### PayPal Sandbox Accounts
```
Business Account:
Email: sandbox@example.com
Password: provided in dev docs

Buyer Account:
Email: buyer@sandbox.paypal.com
Password: Test1234
```

### Bitcoin Testnet
```
Testnet Explorer: https://mempool.space/testnet
Testnet Faucet: https://testnet-faucet.mempool.space/
Testnet addresses start with 'm' or 'n'
```

## Production Deployment

Before deploying to production:

1. ✅ Replace all `pk_test_` with `pk_live_` (Stripe)
2. ✅ Switch PayPal environment from `sandbox` to `production`
3. ✅ Use production keys for all payment providers
4. ✅ Verify HTTPS on all endpoints
5. ✅ Test with real small transactions
6. ✅ Enable webhook signing verification
7. ✅ Set up monitoring and alerting
8. ✅ Configure rate limiting
9. ✅ Enable PCI DSS compliance checks
10. ✅ Review security audit results

## Security Best Practices

1. **Never commit `.env.local`** - Add to `.gitignore`
2. **Use different keys per environment** - Dev, Staging, Production
3. **Rotate webhook secrets regularly** - At least quarterly
4. **Monitor for unauthorized access** - Check provider dashboards
5. **Enable webhook signature verification** - On backend
6. **Use HTTPS everywhere** - No HTTP for payments
7. **Implement rate limiting** - Prevent abuse
8. **Log transactions securely** - Encrypt sensitive data
9. **Enable fraud detection** - Use provider's fraud tools
10. **Regular security audits** - At least annually

## Verification Checklist

- [ ] All required environment variables are set
- [ ] Environment variables are NOT committed to git
- [ ] Keys are valid for the selected environment (test/production)
- [ ] API endpoint is accessible and responding
- [ ] Webhook endpoints are configured on all providers
- [ ] SSL/TLS certificates are valid
- [ ] CORS is properly configured
- [ ] Rate limiting is enabled
- [ ] Monitoring and alerting are in place
- [ ] Disaster recovery plan is documented

## Support

For environment configuration issues:
1. Check provider's documentation: docs.stripe.com, developer.paypal.com, etc.
2. Review backend logs for API errors
3. Test individual services in isolation
4. Check browser console for client-side errors
5. Verify network requests in browser DevTools

